{
 "description": "desired.v2 §2.17, §5: one reading of one target's role against its author's document -> §5's four questions (converged, refused, last_known, in_force), each an answer (yes, no, not_yet, unobservable, not_asked) and a reason. Computed twice by two scripts of the text's drafter that share no code, kept out of the repository, and never blessed. reading.target: its presence (present; absent, a complete read without its instance token; incomplete; across_face, where the deployment's word stands for its descriptor); its descriptor ({lists, bound}, or null when not read); deployment, the deployment's word in the same form, read across a face; its report, the reply §2.10 finds ({tag, hex}, read as reports.json's reads are), or null when none was read; age, its report's by the freshness major its contract uses (fresh, stale, unobservable, or null with no horizon). reading.author: its presence (the same four), and get, its answer to S4's GET of the slice: \"not_made\" (no GET, as with no slice); \"timeout\" (ended at its timeout, or with an error); \"silent\" (no reply); \"unstamped\" (a reply with no envelope); {entry: version} (a live entry); {tombstone: version}; {no_entry: run} (a snapshot with no entry, its header's run). Steps 1 to 4 are v1 §2.17's, for every question: target_absent (not asked), presence_incomplete, no_descriptor, not_a_target (not asked), unbound (not asked, but in_force no), no_report (nothing_crossed across a face), report_invalid (unreadable or malformed), report_stale, report_unobservable. Step 5 reads the report's fields: refused, by outcome, not asked with not_acted; last_known; in_force, yes with desired (desired where in_force is not none, else partial), no with the source otherwise. Steps 6 and 7 answer converged: author_absent (not asked), author_presence_incomplete, author_not_read, author_read_incomplete (a timeout, or unstamped), author_silent (no reply; or a snapshot with no entry under another run than the report's observed version's, or with no observed version stated); a snapshot with no entry under the observed version's run: yes reverted where the outcome is reverted, else not_yet behind; an entry or a tombstone: not_yet not_acted with no observed version; the same version, by outcome (yes converged or reverted, no refused or failed); the same run, a lower observed seq not_yet behind, a higher one unobservable ahead; another run not_yet other_epoch.",
